  <prompt>
    Change the framework `pageSize` fallback in `DataGrid.tsx` from `?? 100` to `?? 25` (owner clarification 2026-07-02). Update the doc comment on `DataGridConfiguration.ts:329` to say `Default 25`. Ship a unit test on the fallback. Identify drill-through / full-page consumers that may rely on the old default via grep + note in PR description.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE frontend framework developer. Aware that this is a global behavior change requiring identification of at-risk consumers.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Framework default `pageSize = 25`. Consumers that want 100 must set it explicitly. Doc/code aligned. Unit test verifies fallback. At-risk consumers identified for PR reviewer awareness.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design Issue 8 flagged doc drift: comment says `Default 50 per design.md` but runtime code uses `?? 100`. During `/design-to-spec` interview 2026-07-02, owner clarified: change default to 25 (workspace embedding is dominant use case; drill-through consumers explicitly override). Merges Issue 8 (doc drift fix) and Issue 11 (default decision) into a single code+doc change.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/DataGrid.tsx</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/types/DataGridConfiguration.ts</file>
      <file>docs/guides/DATAGRID-FRAMEWORK-CONFIGURATION-GUIDE.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Framework changes stay in `@spaarke/ui-components`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Unit test framework-contract; MAINTAIN-class.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Additive-safe: existing config records with explicit `pageSize` set are unaffected; only records that omit `pageSize` see the new default.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The 6 workspace-widget config records currently set `pageSize: 25` explicitly — no functional change for them.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2/spec.md</file>
