    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read spec.md § FR-07 + owner clarifications table. Confirm target: `?? 100` → `?? 25`.</step>
    <step order="2">Locate `DataGrid.tsx` line ~847 (`?? 100`). Change to `?? 25`.</step>
    <step order="3">Update `DataGridConfiguration.ts:329` JSDoc comment for `behavior.pageSize` field: `Default 25 (workspace-widget majority use case). Drill-through / full-page consumers should override explicitly to 50 or 100.`</step>
    <step order="4">Add unit test on `DataGrid` component (or extract the fallback into a helper for testability): assert that when `config.behavior.pageSize` is undefined, the effective pageSize passed to fetch is 25.</step>
    <step order="5">Grep for `sprk_gridconfiguration` records in the codebase (test fixtures, documentation examples) with omitted `pageSize`. List them in the PR description for reviewer awareness — none should exist as production records, but document the search.</step>
    <step order="6">Update `docs/guides/DATAGRID-FRAMEWORK-CONFIGURATION-GUIDE.md` where it references the pageSize default (search for "pageSize" in that guide). Align text with the new default.</step>
    <step order="7">Run `npm test` — all pass; new test passes.</step>
    <step order="8">Run `npm run build` — build succeeds.</step>
    <step order="9">Update TASK-INDEX.md: status → ✅ completed.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build and test</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Grep for at-risk consumers</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/DataGrid.tsx (modified)</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/types/DataGridConfiguration.ts (modified comment)</output>
