    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/__tests__/DataGrid.pageSize.test.ts (new or extended)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a config record with `behavior.pageSize` undefined, when the DataGrid renders, then the effective pageSize is 25 (not 100).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a config record with `behavior.pageSize: 50` (or any explicit value), when the DataGrid renders, then the explicit value is used (not overridden by the new default).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Doc comment on `DataGridConfiguration.ts` says `Default 25`. Configuration guide reflects the same.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm test` and `npm run build` clean.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    - The 6 existing entity-list widgets ship with explicit `pageSize: 25` in their config records — this change is invisible to them.
    - Post-change, those explicit settings could be removed (rely on new default), but that's optional cleanup — leave them for now to keep PR 1 focused.
    - Reviewer note in PR description: this is a global default change. Grep in step 5 should confirm no production record relies on the old default of 100. If any is found, either explicitly set `pageSize: 100` on that record OR flag for reviewer discussion.
  </notes>

